  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and the full test suite passes (1915 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I haven't committed anything.\n\n`@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())` now turns `key=value` into a `(key, value)` tuple:\n\n- **Valid input:** the string is split at the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`. An empty value is allowed: `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Invalid input:** anything with no `=` or an empty key (`abc`, `=v`, `=`, an empty string) fails with `'abc' is not a valid key=value pair.` and exits with code 2.\n- **Tuples:** a value that is already a tuple, such as a default, is passed through unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/click/types.py`:** the new `KeyValue` class, placed after `UUIDParameterType`.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`:** exports `KeyValue`.\n- **Docs:** added `KeyValue` to `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** the latest section (8.5.0) is already released, so I started a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" section for this entry. Change the version number if you're planning a different release.\n- **`tests/test_types.py`:** tests for valid and invalid inputs, plus a command-line test using `--set` with `multiple=True` and the `--set foo` error case.",
